{"id":"12c3a9e7-f3d0-46e8-8b6d-16ea333c2d84","object":"chat.completion","created":1784883366,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    edges = []\\n    for d in distances:\\n        u, v, dist = d\\n        if u < v:\\n            a, b = u, v\\n        else:\\n            a, b = v, u\\n        w = max(core[u], core[v], dist)\\n        edges.append((w, a, b))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, a, b in edges:\\n        if union(a, b):\\n            mst_edges.append([a, b, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is not connected')\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that computes MST on mutual reachability graph. Input case contains nodes list, core_distance dict, distances list of triples (node1, node2, distance). Need to compute mutual reachability for each pair as max(core_dist[node1], core_dist[node2], distance). Then construct edges with weight = mutual_reachability, undirected (so we can canonicalize by sorting node names). Then sort edges by weight, then by node1, then node2 (assuming string comparison). Then run Kruskal's algorithm with union-find to get MST edges (n-1 edges). Add total weight. Output JSON with mst_edges (list of [node1, node2, weight]) and total_weight. Make sure to use only standard library, no randomness. Ensure deterministic tie-breaking.\n\nAlso need to handle potential disconnected graph: if MST cannot be formed (graph not connected) then raise ValueError? The spec says reject disconnected inputs, and raise ValueError for infeasible. So if after processing all edges, we have fewer than n-1 edges, raise ValueError.\n\nWe must not mutate input. So copy distances or just process.\n\nImplement union-find with path compression and union by rank.\n\nOutput must match schema: mst_edges array of arrays each with 3 elements (string, string, number). total_weight number.\n\nAlso note that case might have nodes that are not in distances? But distances list should cover all pairs? Actually not necessarily all pairs, but MST requires fully connected graph. If some pairs missing, it's disconnected, raise ValueError.\n\nImplementation plan:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case['nodes']\n    core = case['core_distance']\n    distances = case['distances']\n    n = len(nodes)\n    # Build map from sorted tuple to mutual reachability weight\n    # Edge list: (weight, node1, node2)\n    edges = []\n    for d in distances:\n        u, v, dist = d\n        # canonicalize\n        if u < v:\n            a, b = u, v\n        else:\n            a, b = v, u\n        core_u = core[u]\n        core_v = core[v]\n        w = max(core_u, core_v, dist)\n        edges.append((w, a, b))\n    # sort by weight, then a, then b\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\n    # union-find\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\n            parent[rx] = ry\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n        else:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    mst_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n    for w, a, b in edges:\n        if union(a, b):\n            mst_edges.append([a, b, w])\n            total_weight += w\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\n                break\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Graph is not connected\")\n    # Ensure mst_edges are in canonical form already\n    # Return dict\n    return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total_weight}\n\nThat should work.\n\nNow need to output as JSON with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source string. Must escape properly.\n\nWrite the source code as a string. Ensure no extra spaces/tabs.\n\nLet's produce the response."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2017,"completion_tokens":1277,"total_tokens":3294,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":842},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":2017},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}